# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GENERATED AND VENDORED FILES  (#346)
#
# WHY. This repo commits its build output, because the MAUI app loads the built
# HTML as a packaged asset — the C# side reads `Spixi/Resources/Raw/html`, so the
# artefacts have to be in the tree. The cost is that a reviewer opening the repo
# on GitHub sees generated bytes and vendored libraries counted as authored work,
# and every pull request that rebuilds shows tens of thousands of changed lines
# that nobody can read.
#
# `linguist-generated=true` collapses these files in diffs and drops them from the
# repository language statistics. `-diff` also keeps `git diff` from printing them
# locally. Neither flag changes what is committed, packaged or shipped — this is a
# presentation setting only.
#
# Context: #345 already removed ~432,000 lines of this problem by shipping the
# shared payload once instead of inlining it into all 22 shells. This finishes the
# job for what remains.
#
# ⚠ MAINTENANCE. The rule below marks EVERY .html in the built output directory,
# then un-marks the eight legacy hand-authored pages by name. If a legacy page is
# retired (settings_lock.html is already slated), delete its line. If a new shell
# is added to build-shells.mjs, nothing needs to change.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Built shells and the six shared assets emitted beside them (#345).
Spixi/Resources/Raw/html/*.html   linguist-generated=true -diff
Spixi/Resources/Raw/html/spixi.*.js    linguist-generated=true -diff
Spixi/Resources/Raw/html/spixi.*.css   linguist-generated=true -diff

# …except these eight, which are hand-authored legacy pages, not build output.
# A later pattern wins in .gitattributes, so these restore normal diffs.
Spixi/Resources/Raw/html/address.html                 -linguist-generated diff
Spixi/Resources/Raw/html/apps.html                    -linguist-generated diff
Spixi/Resources/Raw/html/settings_lock.html           -linguist-generated diff
Spixi/Resources/Raw/html/wallet_contact_request.html  -linguist-generated diff
Spixi/Resources/Raw/html/wallet_recipient.html        -linguist-generated diff
Spixi/Resources/Raw/html/wallet_request.html          -linguist-generated diff
Spixi/Resources/Raw/html/wallet_send.html             -linguist-generated diff
Spixi/Resources/Raw/html/wallet_send_2.html           -linguist-generated diff

# Generated bundles consumed by the demos and inlined/emitted by build-shells.
src/demo/spixi.iife.js         linguist-generated=true -diff
src/demo/strings.iife.js       linguist-generated=true -diff
src/components/icons.iife.js   linguist-generated=true -diff
src/components/icons.js        linguist-generated=true -diff
src/styles/chat-pattern.css    linguist-generated=true -diff

# Generated string dictionaries. The AUTHORED sources are src/strings/en-us.json
# and the inline `strings.KEY || 'fallback'` defaults inside the components —
# every .js file here is written by scripts/extract-strings.mjs and
# scripts/build-locales.mjs. Editing one by hand is a known trap (#341 lesson 1).
src/strings/*.js               linguist-generated=true -diff
# …except the provider, which is hand-authored. It is the only entry point the
# pseudo-locale leak test has, so its diffs must stay readable (#346 review).
src/strings/index.js           -linguist-generated diff

# Third-party libraries shipped verbatim. Vendored, not written here.
Spixi/Resources/Raw/html/js/bootstrap.min.js    linguist-vendored=true -diff
Spixi/Resources/Raw/html/js/clipboard.min.js    linguist-vendored=true -diff
Spixi/Resources/Raw/html/js/html5-qrcode.min.js linguist-vendored=true -diff
Spixi/Resources/Raw/html/js/jquery.min.js       linguist-vendored=true -diff
Spixi/Resources/Raw/html/js/qrcode.min.js       linguist-vendored=true -diff
Spixi/Resources/Raw/html/css/bootstrap.min.css  linguist-vendored=true -diff
Spixi/Resources/Raw/html/css/normalize.css      linguist-vendored=true -diff

# RocksDB, vendored as a prebuilt native dependency. The binaries are already
# excluded from the language statistics because they are binary, but the 238
# checked-in C headers are TEXT — without this the repository reports itself as
# largely a C project, which is the single most misleading thing about it.
Spixi/Platforms/iOS/NativeLibraries/**   linguist-vendored=true -diff
Spixi/Platforms/Android/lib/**           linguist-vendored=true -diff
local-nuget/**                           linguist-vendored=true -diff
local-nuget/README.md                    -linguist-vendored diff

# ⚠ `-diff` means `git diff` prints "Binary files … differ" for these paths. This
# project ships changes to the owner's machine as patches — use `git diff --binary`
# or `git format-patch --binary` for any hand-off that touches a marked file, or a
# tarball, which is what the workflow already does for generated output.
